#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""re-fingerprint — RE target fingerprinter (wq#5200, Limpet capability router stage 1).

Input : a file path.
Output: JSON {format, arch, os, vendor_hints, embedded_formats, ...} on stdout.

Sources, in order of trust:
  1. container/header parsers (ELF, PE, Mach-O, APK/ZIP, DEX, FDT/DTB, Android boot,
     Rockchip RKFW/RKAF/RKNS, uImage, Android sparse, LiME, Windows crash dump)
  2. signature sweep over the whole file (offset, validated) -> embedded_formats,
     recursing into gzip/xz/lzma/bzip2/zstd payloads up to --depth (nested firmware)
  3. `file -b` and `binwalk` signature scan (when installed; read-only, timed)
  4. vendor / OS strings (U-Boot, Linux version, Android build props, RTOS banners, SoC ids)

`format` uses re-route's vocabulary (ELF PE Mach-O APK DEX JAR HBC PYC Godot_PCK firmware
memory_dump unknown) and `conditions` matches routing.rules augments in
/home/lumen/re/toolkit-expansion/capability-registry.json, so a fingerprint routes 1:1.

Read-only: never writes, never executes the target.
"""
